    "result_text": "Typecheck passes cleanly. The change is complete and the acceptance test is green.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe change request \u2014 *\"Let me change or remove those charge lines on an invoice. Update the total when I do.\"* \u2014 as an additive full-stack change:\n\n**Server (OfficeFloor REST)** \u2014 two new endpoints, each recomputing the invoice's derived `amount` from its remaining lines and auditing the action:\n- `POST /api/lineitems/remove` \u2014 `LineItemsRemove` + `RemoveLineItem` body + `lineitems/remove.POST.yml`. Deletes the line, recomputes the total, records `LINE_ITEM_REMOVED`.\n- `POST /api/lineitems/edit` \u2014 `LineItemsEdit` + `EditLineItem` body + `lineitems/edit.POST.yml`. Applies the same validation as adding, recomputes the total, records `LINE_ITEM_UPDATED`.\n\n**Front-end** \u2014 edited only the feature's own `InvoiceLineItemsPanel.tsx` (not a page or shared slot region). Each line now has:\n- a **Remove** button (`lineitem-remove-${id}`) \u2192 remove mutation,\n- an **Edit** button (`lineitem-edit-${id}`) that opens in-place inputs (`lineitem-edit-description/qty/unitprice-${id}`) with **Save**/**Cancel** \u2192 edit mutation.\n\nBoth writes `invalidateQueries` on `['lineItems']` and `['invoices']`, so the list refetches and `invoice-amount` recomputes \u2014 sharing keys rather than hand-maintaining state (rule 5). The only `useState` is the add form and the line currently being edited (rule 4).\n\n**No migration needed** \u2014 the `line_item` table already supports delete/update, and V15 had already dropped the positive-amount constraint, so a line can be removed even down to a zero total.\n\nThe existing `data-testid` anchors (`invoice-amount`, `lineitem-row-${id}`, etc.) are all preserved; the test verifies removing \"Hosting\" drops the total from `$150.00` to `$100.00`.",
